 "notes": {
  "application": [
   {
    "text": "Input: ceramic decoupling capacitor over 10 uF; optional 0.1 uF VIN-GND for high frequency; voltage rating above the maximum input.",
    "ref": {
     "page": 15,
     "quote": "TI recommends a ceramic capacitor over 10µF for the decoupling capacitor.",
     "mode": "raw"
    }
   },
   {
    "text": "Feedback: R2 (top) about 100 k; TI's 5 V example uses R2 100 k and R3 13.3 k (VREF 0.596 V typ).",
    "ref": {
     "page": 15,
     "quote": "Select a value of R2 to be approximately 100kΩ.",
     "mode": "raw"
    }
   },
   {
    "text": "Inductor: LMIN = VIN(MAX) x KIND x IOUT x fsw relation (Equation in 7.2.3); KIND = ripple / max output current.",
    "ref": {
     "page": 16,
     "quote": "KIND is a coefficient that represents the amount of inductor ripple current relative to the maximum output",
     "mode": "raw"
    }
   },
   {
    "text": "EN has an internal pull-up current: floating EN enables the device.",
    "ref": {
     "page": 10,
     "quote": "The EN pin has an internal pullup-current source which allows the user to float the EN pin to enable the device.",
     "mode": "raw"
    }
   },
   {
    "text": "If the supply is more than a few inches away, add bulk capacitance (47 uF electrolytic typical).",
    "ref": {
     "page": 21,
     "quote": "An electrolytic capacitor with a",
     "mode": "raw"
    }
   }
  ],
  "layout": [
   {
    "text": "VIN and GND traces as wide as possible; input and output capacitors as close to the device as possible with sufficient vias.",
    "ref": {
     "page": 21,
     "quote": "The VIN and GND traces should be as wide as possible to reduce trace impedance.",
     "mode": "raw"
    }
   },
   {
    "text": "SW trace short and wide; no switching current under the device.",
    "ref": {
     "page": 21,
     "quote": "Do not allow switching current to flow under the device.",
     "mode": "raw"
    }
   },
